      {
        "id": 129246,
        "name": "Deimir",
        "username": "Deimir",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/ecb155/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-27T21:15:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And the videos they release will only be the ones from the main board, not all of them.Still, Tachyon was livestreamed and was critical to one of the matches, getting two turns in a row that at the very end that got an incap and did enough damage to another character (3/4 on Unity) that the team squeaked out the win on damage ratios.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Much of my time at the screen on the show floor was spent explaining the game mechanics to passersby, but I did manage to see the end of this game. Was pretty exciting seeing one of my thematically favorite characters make so much of a dent in the other team. Next time, I'm hoping to see Absolute Zero make more appearances at the main table.</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
